}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","title":"MXLElision","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision","abstract":[{"text":"The elision type represents an elision between lyric syllables. The text content specifies the symbol used to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"display the elision. Common values are a no-break space (Unicode 00A0), an underscore (Unicode 005F), or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undertie (Unicode 203F). If the text content is empty, the smufl attribute is used to specify the symbol to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use. Its value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics. The SMuFL attribute is ignored if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elision glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor a smufl attribute are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"present, the elision glyph is application-specific.","type":"text"}]}}}